      "text": "To find the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of these two numbers. The GCD of two numbers is the largest positive integer that divides both numbers without leaving a remainder.\n\nFirst, we will factorize 342 and 285 into their prime factors:\n\n- The prime factorization of 342:\n\\[ 342 = 2 \\times 171 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 57 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 19 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19 \\]\n\n- The prime factorization of 285:\n\\[ 285 = 3 \\times 95 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19 \\]\n\nNext, we identify the common prime factors. The common prime factors of 342 and 285 are 3 and 19. Therefore, the GCD of 342 and 285 is:\n\\[ \\text{GCD}(342, 285) = 3 \\times 19 = 57 \\]\n\nThus, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is \\(\\boxed{57}\\).",
