    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "First, we need to find the prime factorizations of 342 and 285.\n\nFor 342, we divide by the smallest prime numbers:\n\\[\n342 \\div 2 = 171\n\\]\n\\[\n171 \\div 3 = 57\n\\]\n\\[\n57 \\div 3 = 19\n\\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 342 is:\n\\[\n342 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19\n\\]\n\nFor 285, we do the same:\n\\[\n285 \\div 3 = 95\n\\]\n\\[\n95 \\div 5 = 19\n\\]\nSo, the prime factorization of 285 is:\n\\[\n285 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the common factors of 342 and 285. The common factors are the prime factors that appear in both factorizations. The prime factorizations are:\n\\[\n342 = 2^1 \\times 3^2 \\times 19^1\n\\]\n\\[\n285 = 3^1 \\times 5^1 \\times 19^1\n\\]\nThe only common factor is 19. Therefore, the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 342 and 285 is 19.\n\nThus, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{19}\n\\]",
